        "content": "# 🔄 Data Routing Strategy\n\n## Lambda Architecture - 48-Hour Cutoff Rule\n\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-around; align-items: center; margin: 20px 0;\">\n\n### 📊 Batch Layer\n**Data Age:** > 48 hours  \n**Purpose:** Historical accuracy  \n**Update:** Daily  \n**Documents:** ~5,000+\n\n### ⚡ Speed Layer  \n**Data Age:** ≤ 48 hours  \n**Purpose:** Real-time freshness  \n**Update:** Every 5 minutes  \n**Documents:** ~500\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Query Routing Logic\n\n| Data Age | Route To | Reason |\n|----------|----------|--------|\n| **Older than 48h** | 📊 **Batch Layer** | Stable, aggregated historical data |\n| **Within 48h** | ⚡ **Speed Layer** | Fresh, real-time updates |\n| **Overlapping** | ⚡ **Speed Layer Priority** | Latest data wins |\n\n---\n\n## 🔀 Data Flow\n\n```\n    User Query\n        |\n        ↓\n   Query Router ← Checks timestamp against 48h cutoff\n        |\n        ├─→ [> 48h] → Batch Layer (MongoDB: batch_views)\n        |\n        └─→ [≤ 48h] → Speed Layer (MongoDB: speed_views)\n        |\n        ↓\n   View Merger ← Combines results if needed\n        |\n        ↓\n   Unified Response\n```\n\n**Current Cutoff Time:** Check panel above  \n**Configuration:** 48 hours (configurable in query router)",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
